    "jays": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Blue Jays",
      "league": "MLB",
      "record": "29-30",
      "detail": "3rd in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays keep finding new ways to make life hard on themselves, and last night they let one slip through their fingers in the ugliest fashion imaginable. <strong>Toronto was beaten 6-5 by Baltimore after a five-run ninth inning blew up the lead</strong>, a collapse that snapped the club's four-game winning streak and left it sitting at 29-30, third in the AL East, 8 games back and 6th in the playoff picture. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. at least did his part - he had his first four-hit game since Sept. 5 - and that is the sort of bright spot a club clinging to relevance has to grab. But the bigger story is the same one that has dogged this team for weeks: too many missed chances, too little finish. The margin between respectable and frustrating is still paper-thin in this race, and Toronto is living on that edge. <strong>Next comes another shot at Baltimore this morning at 11:15 AM ET, and the Blue Jays need a cleaner closing act than the one they staged Saturday night</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated May 31, 2026"
      },
