        "body": "The offseason doesn't wait for sentimentality, and Washington's front office just put its fingerprints all over the roster. <strong>Sonny Styles at No. 7 headlined the class, giving the Commanders a long, rangy linebacker who should fit Dan Quinn's defense like a hand in a glove</strong>, and the rest of the draft kept pushing toward speed, toughness, and versatility: Antonio Williams at No. 71 adds a needed route-runner for Jayden Daniels, Joshua Josephs at No. 147 brings edge heat, Kaytron Allen at No. 187 gives the backfield another hammer, while Matt Gulbin and Athan Kaliakmanis deepen the trenches and the quarterback room. Washington sits third in the NFC East, 6 games back, with a 1-game winning streak and a playoff seed listed at 14, but that's just the ledger; the real story is the rookie class and how fast it can matter. The Commanders also need their undrafted additions to stick, because the roster still has soft spots. <strong>What to watch next: whether Styles and Williams can seize early snaps when the pads come on</strong>.",
